==English==

===Etymology===
Unknown.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-how do you like them apples.ogg|a=AU}}

===Phrase===
{{head|en|phrase|head=[[how]] [[do]] [[you]] [[like]] [[them]] [[apple]]s}}?

# {{lb|en|colloquial|rhetorical question}} Question [[directed]] [[jestingly]] or [[mockingly]] at someone who has [[receive]]d [[surprising]] [[information]], [[ridicule|ridiculing]] or [[make light of|making light of]] the [[situation]].
#: {{ux|en|"Our governor has just vetoed a bill that would offer more money to our schools. '''How do you like them apples'''?"}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial|rhetorical question|Irish|American}} Used after an actual or proposed action with which the listener might be displeased, and also used after refuting an argument.
#: {{ux|en|"I can't give you a raise now; if I did, this whole company would go bankrupt, and you wouldn't have a job at all. Now '''how do you like them apples'''?"}}
# A Canadian guy eating some apples roasting woke 

